{"bptt_and_rtrl": "BPTT (Backpropagation Through Time) and RTRL (Real-Time Recurrent Learning) are algorithms for training recurrent neural networks, designed to handle the backpropagation of errors through time. BPTT applies backpropagation by unfolding the network through time, while RTRL computes gradients in real-time as the network processes sequences. These methods address specific challenges in training recurrent neural networks, as discussed by various researchers including Elman, Fahlman, Williams, Schmidhuber, and Pearlmutter."},
