{"net_input": "The net input refers to the total input received by a recurrent unit in a neural network, which is a combination of external inputs and feedback from other units.|Here is another description: The net input refers to the total input received by a neuron or a processing unit in a neural network, which is crucial for determining the output signal.|Here is another description: The net input refers to the total input received by a memory cell in a neural network, specifically the _v_ th memory cell of memory cell block _cj_. It is a crucial component in determining the internal state and output activation of the cell.|Here is another description: The net input is the cumulative sum of weighted inputs to the memory cell, which includes contributions from previous cell states and current inputs. It serves as a foundational value in determining the dynamics of the memory cell's internal state and output activation.|Here is another description: The net input refers to the total input received by a unit in a neural network, which is crucial for determining the activation level of that unit."},
