{"ring": "Ring refers to a researcher, specifically Ring (1993), who contributed to the field by developing a unique approach to address time lags in neural networks.|Here is another description: Ring refers to the approach proposed by Ring in 1993 for bridging long time lags in neural networks. This method involves specific mechanisms to handle conflicting error signals within the network."},
