{"error__propagated_back_into_time_for__q_time_steps": "The predicate \"propagated back into time for\" describes the process by which the error at a particular unit and time step is traced back through the network over a series of time steps. This backward propagation is essential for understanding how errors accumulate and influence the learning process in recurrent neural networks."},
{"q_time_steps": "The object \"q time steps\" specifies the duration over which the error is propagated backward in time. This parameter _q_ determines how far back in the sequence the error is considered, influencing the scaling factor applied to the error as it is backpropagated through the network.|Here is another description: The object \"_q_ time steps\" represents the specific duration or number of discrete intervals over which the error signal is scaled as it flows through the memory cell."},
{"error__propagated_to__unit_v": "The predicate \"propagated to\" describes the process by which the error at one unit in the neural network is transmitted or extended to another unit. This propagation is a key aspect of the backpropagation algorithm, allowing the network to learn from its mistakes by adjusting the weights based on the errors that have been distributed across the network."},
