{"inj_outj": "The gate units _inj_ and _outj_ are integral parts of the memory cell _cj_, responsible for opening and closing access to the CEC. They ensure that the information flow is managed effectively within the system, allowing for controlled interaction with the memory cell."},
{"self_recurrent_connection": "The self-recurrent connection is a feedback loop within the architecture of the memory cell, specifically within the CEC (Cellular Exponential Cell) framework. It is designed to provide feedback with a delay of one time step, which is crucial for the functioning of the memory cell.|Here is another description: The self-recurrent connection is a feature within the architecture of a memory cell, specifically noted for having a weight of 1.0. It is integral to the functioning of the CEC (presumably a type of memory or processing unit).|Here is another description: The self-recurrent connection is a feedback loop within the memory cell architecture, characterized by a weight of 1.0 and a delay of one time step."},
