{"different_error_signals": "Different error signals refer to various types of error information that can be transmitted within a neural network. These signals are crucial for the network's learning process, as they help adjust the weights and biases to minimize errors during training.|Here is another description: Different error signals refer to various distinct error signals that are generated and transmitted within a system, particularly in the context of memory cells and their operations."},
{"different_error_signals__flowing_into__the_cell_at_different_times_via_its_output_gate": "Flowing into describes the process by which error signals are transmitted or propagated into a specific component of the neural network. This propagation is essential for the network to update its parameters based on the error information received."},
{"the_cell_at_different_times_via_its_output_gate": "The cell (at different times) via its output gate refers to a memory cell in a neural network that receives error signals through its output gate at various points in time. The output gate controls the flow of information in and out of the cell, allowing it to manage when and how error signals are integrated into the cell's state."},
