{"output_gate": "The output gate is a critical component in neural network architectures, particularly in gated recurrent units (GRUs) and long short-term memory (LSTM) networks. It controls the flow of information, determining when and how data is transmitted within the system, and which parts of the cell state are output at each time step. This mechanism ensures that certain learned elements do not interfere with others and manages the release of information from memory cells."},
