{"error_signal__arrives_at__memory_cell_output": "The arrival of the error signal at the memory cell output signifies the point where the signal is received and prepared for further processing within the memory cell."},
{"memory_cell_output": "The memory cell output is the point where the error signal is received and subsequently scaled by output gate activation and _h_ [\u2032], initiating its journey within the memory cell\u2019s CEC.|Here is another description: The memory cell output is the result or signal produced by a memory cell, which is a fundamental component in certain types of neural networks, particularly in architectures like Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks.|Here is another description: The memory cell output is a component within the neural network or computational model where data or signals are produced as a result of the memory cell's operations. It is the target location where the error _\u03d1j_ is received."},
{"error_signal__gets_scaled_by__output_gate_activation_and_h": "The process of getting scaled involves adjusting the magnitude of the error signal based on certain factors. This scaling is essential for controlling the impact of the error signal on the memory cell\u2019s operations and ensuring stability in the system."},
{"output_gate_activation_and_h": "The output gate activation and _h_ [\u2032] are components that influence the scaling of the error signal. The output gate activation determines how much of the error signal is allowed to pass through, while _h_ [\u2032] likely represents a state or condition within the memory cell that further modulates the error signal."},
{"error_signal__is_within__memory_cell_s_cec": "The predicate \"is within\" describes the state of the error signal being located inside the memory cell\u2019s CEC, where it can circulate without further scaling."},
{"memory_cell_s_cec": "The memory cell\u2019s CEC is a component within the memory cell where the error signal can flow back indefinitely without being scaled, playing a crucial role in the error signal's processing.|Here is another description: The memory cell\u2019s CEC (Constant Error Carousel) is a mechanism within a memory cell of a neural network that is designed to maintain a constant flow of error signals. This helps in stabilizing the learning process by ensuring that errors are consistently propagated without significant alteration as they pass through the memory cell."},
{"error_signal__can_flow_back__indefinitely_without_ever_being_scaled": "The predicate \"can flow back\" describes the behavior of the error signal within the memory cell's CEC (Cellular Encoding Circuit), indicating that the signal has the capability to circulate or propagate within this specific component without undergoing any scaling process."},
{"indefinitely_without_ever_being_scaled": "The object \"indefinitely without ever being scaled\" refers to the characteristic of the error signal within the memory cell\u2019s CEC, where it is able to circulate continuously without any scaling adjustments being applied to it."},
{"error_signal__leaves_the_memory_cell_through__input_gate_and_g": "The phrase \"leaves the memory cell through\" describes the pathway or process by which the error signal exits the memory cell. This exit is necessary for the signal to influence other components of the system, such as adjusting incoming weights."},
{"input_gate_and_g": "The input gate and _g_ are components within the memory cell that regulate the flow of information. The input gate controls the extent to which new information is allowed to enter the cell, while _g_ likely represents a specific parameter or function associated with the gate's operation."},
{"error_signal__is_scaled_once_more_by__input_gate_activation_and_g": "The phrase \"is scaled once more by\" indicates a secondary scaling process that the error signal undergoes. This scaling is essential for modulating the signal's impact as it interacts with other components within the memory cell."},
{"input_gate_activation_and_g": "The input gate activation and _g_ [\u2032] represent the components responsible for the final scaling of the error signal before it affects the incoming weights. These elements play a critical role in determining how the error signal influences the memory cell's learning process."},
{"error_signal__serves_to__change_the_incoming_weights": "The phrase \"serves to\" indicates the purpose or function of the error signal within the system. In this context, it describes how the error signal is utilized to make necessary adjustments to enhance the accuracy and efficiency of the memory cell's operations."},
{"change_the_incoming_weights": "The incoming weights refer to the parameters within the memory cell that determine the strength of the connections between different components. Changing these weights based on the error signal allows the system to adapt and learn from previous errors, thereby improving its overall performance and accuracy."},
