{"all_our_experiments__use__online_learning_as_opposed_to_batch_learning_and_logistic_sigmoids_as_activation_functions": "The use of online learning and logistic sigmoids as activation functions in these experiments signifies the methodological approach taken to process and learn from the data in real-time, as opposed to batch processing, and to apply a specific type of mathematical function to determine the output of neural network nodes."},
{"online_learning_as_opposed_to_batch_learning_and_logistic_sigmoids_as_activation_functions": "Online learning, as opposed to batch learning, and logistic sigmoids as activation functions represent the specific techniques and functions employed in the experiments. Online learning allows for the model to update its parameters incrementally as new data arrives, while logistic sigmoids provide a smooth, S-shaped curve to map the input to an output between 0 and 1, facilitating the learning process in neural networks."},
