{"training_sequences_with_short_time_lags": "Training sequences with short time lags refer to the input sequences used in the training process of recurrent neural networks, where the time intervals between relevant events or symbols are relatively brief. These sequences are crucial for evaluating the network's ability to learn and process information effectively within short temporal windows.|Here is another description: Training sequences with short time lags refer to sequences where the time interval between consecutive elements is relatively small, as few as nine steps in this context. These sequences are used to train the neural network in predicting the next symbol in the string."},
