{"truly_beneficial_in_the_embedded_reber_grammar": "The embedded Reber grammar is a standard benchmark test used to evaluate the performance of recurrent neural networks. It involves sequences with short time lags and is utilized to demonstrate the effectiveness of LSTM networks, particularly highlighting the advantages offered by LSTM\u2019s output gates."},
{"experiment_2": "Experiment 2 is a specific study within a series of experiments designed to test the capabilities of different neural network architectures, particularly focusing on their performance in handling complex sequence processing tasks."},
