{"training_exemplars": "Training exemplars refer to specific instances or examples selected for use in the training process of a machine learning model. In this context, they are part of a local input-output representation used to train the model.|Here is another description: Training exemplars refer to the specific instances or examples selected for use in training a model or system. In this context, they are sequences that are used to train a predictive model.|Here is another description: Training exemplars refer to the specific instances or examples selected from a dataset to train a machine learning model. In this context, they are sequences chosen to help the model learn to predict the next element in a series."},
