{"after_string_presentation": "The subject refers to the phase immediately following the presentation of a string in a machine learning or neural network context. This is a critical moment where the system processes the input and prepares for the next step."},
{"after_string_presentation__all_activations_are__reinitialized_with_zeros": "The predicate describes the action taken by the system after a string is presented. Specifically, it indicates that all activations within the system are reset. This is a common practice to ensure that the network does not carry over any residual information from previous inputs, thereby maintaining the integrity of the current input processing."},
