{"the_minimal_time_lag": "The minimal time lag refers to the shortest duration between two events or data points in a sequence that is necessary for effective processing or analysis.|Here is another description: The minimal time lag represents the shortest duration between consecutive elements in a sequence that the model can effectively process. This parameter is crucial for ensuring that the model can capture the temporal dependencies within the sequences it analyzes.|Here is another description: The minimal time lag is a parameter that represents the shortest duration between events or data points in a sequence, crucial for the evaluation and testing of sequences."},
