{"the_net__never_sees__short_training_sequences": "The phrase \"never sees\" indicates a limitation or characteristic of the neural network where it is not exposed to or does not utilize certain types of data during its operation."},
{"short_training_sequences": "Short training sequences are brief data inputs used for training machine learning models. In this context, they are specifically excluded from the neural network's training process to enhance its performance on longer sequences.|Here is another description: Short training sequences refer to brief segments of data used in the training phase of a machine learning model. These sequences are typically limited in length and are designed to provide the model with initial patterns and features to learn from."},
{"short_training_sequences__facilitating__the_classification_of_long_test_sequences": "Facilitating in this context means aiding or making easier. It describes the role that short training sequences play in helping the model to perform a specific task more effectively."},
{"the_classification_of_long_test_sequences": "The classification of long test sequences involves using a trained model to categorize or label extended data sequences that were not part of the training set. These sequences are longer and more complex, requiring the model to generalize from what it learned during training."},
{"twenty_trials": "Twenty trials refer to a series of experiments or tests conducted to evaluate the performance or outcomes of certain conditions or variables. In this context, these trials are part of a study or research aimed at assessing specific pairs."},
