{"first_n_real_valued_sequence_elements": "The first N real-valued sequence elements refer to the initial part of an input sequence that is crucial for the classification task. These elements are specifically selected to provide meaningful data points that help in determining the class to which the sequence belongs."},
{"first_n_real_valued_sequence_elements__convey__relevant_information_about_the_class": "The predicate \"convey\" in this context means that the first N real-valued sequence elements are used to transmit or provide essential data that is necessary for making an accurate classification decision. These elements are the carriers of the critical information needed to distinguish between the two classes."},
{"relevant_information_about_the_class": "Relevant information about the class pertains to the specific data or characteristics that are necessary to correctly classify the input sequence into one of the two possible classes. This information is encoded within the first N elements of the sequence and is vital for achieving accurate classification results."},
{"sequence_elements_at_positions_t_n": "The subject refers to the sequence elements that appear at positions greater than a specified value N in a given sequence. These elements are part of a two-sequence problem where the classification of sequences is based on the first N elements."},
