{"task_3c__has__targets_0_2_and_0_8_for_class_1_and_class_2_respectively": "The predicate \"has\" in this context signifies that Task 3c is characterized by specific targets for its classes. These targets are essential parameters that the system must learn to minimize mean squared error and achieve acceptable network output."},
{"targets_0_2_and_0_8_for_class_1_and_class_2_respectively": "The targets 0.2 and 0.8 for class 1 and class 2, respectively, are specific output values that the system aims to achieve in Task 3c. These targets are crucial for defining misclassification and determining the acceptability of the network output, which must have a mean absolute difference below 0.015 from the noise-free target."},
{"task_3c__has__gaussian_noise_on_the_targets_mean_0_and_variance_0_1_s_d_0_32": "The predicate \"has\" in this context indicates that Task 3c includes or is characterized by the presence of gaussian noise on the targets. This noise adds complexity to the task, requiring the system to learn the conditional expectations of the targets given the inputs to minimize mean squared error."},
{"gaussian_noise_on_the_targets_mean_0_and_variance_0_1_s_d_0_32": "The gaussian noise on the targets in Task 3c has a mean of 0 and a variance of 0.1, with a standard deviation of 0.32. This noise affects the target values, making it more difficult for the system to accurately classify inputs and achieve a low mean absolute difference between the noise-free target and the output."},
