{"minimizing_mean_squared_error": "Minimizing mean squared error is a method used in machine learning to optimize model performance by reducing the average of the squared differences between predicted and actual values. In Task 3c, this approach is essential for the system to learn the conditional expectations of the targets given the inputs, ensuring that the output is as close as possible to the noise-free targets."},
{"task_3c__requires__learning_the_conditional_expectations_of_the_targets_given_the_inputs": "The predicate \"requires\" in this context signifies a necessity for the system to perform a specific action or achieve a certain condition to successfully complete Task 3c. It implies that without fulfilling this requirement, the task cannot be considered solved."},
