{"by_means_of_its_recurrent_connections": "The \"recurrent connections\" refer to the feedback loops within the LSTM network that allow information to persist across different time steps. These connections enable Block 1 to continuously check its state, ensuring it can determine if it is empty or filled with data."},
{"block_1__can_close_its_input_gate__after_the_first_x_y_occurs": "The ability of Block 1 to close its input gate signifies a mechanism by which the block can seal itself off from further input after it has stored the initial X or Y. This action is crucial for maintaining the integrity of the stored data and ensuring that the block does not get overwritten by subsequent inputs."},
