{"time_warping_invariant_neural_networks_in_s_j_hanson_j_d_cowan_c_l_giles_eds_advances_in_neural_information_processing_systems_5_pp_180_187_san_mateo_ca_morgan_kaufmann": "\"Time warping invariant neural networks. In S. J. Hanson, J. D. Cowan, & C. L. Giles (Eds.), Advances in neural information processing systems 5 (pp. 180\u2013187). San Mateo, CA: Morgan Kaufmann.\" is the title of the publication where the authors presented their research on time warping invariant neural networks, which was part of the Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 5 conference proceedings."},
{"watrous_r_l_kuhn_g_m": "Watrous, R. L., & Kuhn, G. M. are the authors who contributed to the field of neural networks by proposing a method for inducing finite-state languages."},
{"watrous_r_l_kuhn_g_m__published__induction_of_finite_state_languages_using_second_order_recurrent_networks_neural_computation_4_406_414": "The predicate \"published\" indicates that the authors, Watrous and Kuhn, have made their research findings available to the scientific community through a formal publication."},
{"induction_of_finite_state_languages_using_second_order_recurrent_networks_neural_computation_4_406_414": "\"Induction of finite-state languages using second-order recurrent networks. Neural Computation, 4, 406\u2013414.\" is the title of the research paper published by Watrous and Kuhn in the journal Neural Computation, which presents their work on using second-order recurrent networks for language induction."},
{"werbos_p_j": "Paul J. Werbos is a researcher known for his contributions to the field of neural networks, particularly in the development of backpropagation algorithms."},
{"werbos_p_j__published__generalization_of_backpropagation_with_application_to_a_recurrent_gas_market_model_neural_networks_1_339_356": "The predicate \"published\" indicates that Paul J. Werbos authored and released a specific work in the field of neural networks."},
{"generalization_of_backpropagation_with_application_to_a_recurrent_gas_market_model_neural_networks_1_339_356": "\"Generalization of backpropagation with application to a recurrent gas market model\" is a research paper published in the journal Neural Networks in 1988, where Werbos expanded on the backpropagation algorithm and applied it to a recurrent neural network model for a gas market scenario."},
{"williams_r_j": "R. J. Williams is a researcher who has contributed to the field of neural networks, particularly recurrent neural networks, through various publications and technical reports."},
{"williams_r_j__published__complexity_of_exact_gradient_computation_algorithms_for_recurrent_neural_networks_tech_rep_no_nu_ccs_89_27_boston_northeastern_university_college_of_computer_science": "The predicate \"published\" indicates that R. J. Williams authored and released a technical report that discusses the complexity of exact gradient computation algorithms for recurrent neural networks."},
{"complexity_of_exact_gradient_computation_algorithms_for_recurrent_neural_networks_tech_rep_no_nu_ccs_89_27_boston_northeastern_university_college_of_computer_science": "The technical report titled \"Complexity of exact gradient computation algorithms for recurrent neural networks\" (Tech. Rep. No. NU-CCS-89-27) is a publication by R. J. Williams that explores the computational complexity associated with gradient computation algorithms in the context of recurrent neural networks. It was published by Northeastern University, College of Computer Science in Boston."},
{"williams_r_j_peng_j": "Williams, R. J. & Peng, J. are researchers who have contributed to the field of neural networks, specifically focusing on algorithms for training recurrent networks."},
{"williams_r_j_peng_j__published__an_efficient_gradient_based_algorithm_for_on_line_training_of_recurrent_network_trajectories_neural_computation_4_491_501": "The predicate \"published\" indicates that Williams, R. J. & Peng, J. have authored and released a scientific paper detailing their research findings and methodologies in the field of neural computation."},
{"an_efficient_gradient_based_algorithm_for_on_line_training_of_recurrent_network_trajectories_neural_computation_4_491_501": "\"An efficient gradient-based algorithm for on-line training of recurrent network trajectories. Neural Computation, 4, 491\u2013501.\" is a scientific paper published in the journal Neural Computation, detailing an innovative algorithm developed by Williams, R. J. & Peng, J. for the efficient online training of recurrent neural networks."},
{"williams_r_j_zipser_d": "Williams, R. J., and Zipser, D. are researchers who have contributed to the field of neural networks, particularly in the development of learning algorithms for recurrent networks."},
{"williams_r_j_zipser_d__published__gradient_based_learning_algorithms_for_recurrent_networks_and_their_computational_complexity_in_y_chauvin_d_e_rumelhart_eds_back_propagation_theory_architectures_and_applications_hillsdale_nj_erlbaum": "The predicate \"published\" indicates that the subject, Williams, R. J., and Zipser, D., have authored and released a work, specifically a paper or chapter in a book, that discusses gradient-based learning algorithms for recurrent networks."},
{"gradient_based_learning_algorithms_for_recurrent_networks_and_their_computational_complexity_in_y_chauvin_d_e_rumelhart_eds_back_propagation_theory_architectures_and_applications_hillsdale_nj_erlbaum": "The object \"Gradient-based learning algorithms for recurrent networks and their computational complexity. In Y. Chauvin, & D. E. Rumelhart (Eds.), Back-propagation: Theory, architectures and applications. Hillsdale, NJ: Erlbaum.\" is a publication that presents the research findings of Williams and Zipser on the topic of gradient-based learning algorithms for recurrent networks, including an analysis of their computational complexity. This work was included in an edited volume on back-propagation, a significant concept in neural network training."}
