{"this_article": "This article is a scholarly piece that delves into the challenges and potential solutions related to the use of recurrent networks in various applications such as speech processing and music composition.|Here is another description: This article is a review that discusses the challenges and limitations of using recurrent networks for storing representations of recent input events in the form of activations, particularly in applications like speech processing, non-Markovian control, and music composition.|Here is another description: This article refers to a scholarly work that addresses the challenges faced by conventional recurrent neural network training methods, specifically backpropagation through time (BPTT) and real-time recurrent learning (RTRL)."},
