{"stationary_inputs": "Stationary inputs are a type of input data for neural networks where the statistical properties, such as mean and variance, do not change over time. This contrasts with time-varying inputs, which change over the sequence of data being processed."},
{"gradient_calculations": "Gradient calculations refer to the process of determining the rate of change of a function with respect to its variables, which is crucial in optimizing neural network parameters."},
