{"sun_chen_and_lee_s_alternative_approach": "Sun, Chen, and Lee\u2019s alternative approach is a method proposed in 1993 to address the issue of long time lags in neural networks by modifying the activation of recurrent units."},
{"sun_chen_and_lee_s_alternative_approach__updates__the_activation_of_a_recurrent_unit_by_adding_the_old_activation_and_the_scaled_current_net_input": "The predicate \"updates\" refers to the process by which Sun, Chen, and Lee\u2019s approach modifies the activation levels of recurrent units in a neural network. This is done to better handle long time lags and improve the network's performance."},
{"the_activation_of_a_recurrent_unit_by_adding_the_old_activation_and_the_scaled_current_net_input": "The activation of a recurrent unit by adding the old activation and the (scaled) current net input is a specific method used in Sun, Chen, and Lee\u2019s approach to update the state of recurrent units. This method aims to balance the retention of stored information with the incorporation of new inputs, though it may perturb stored information, making long-term storage challenging."},
{"net_input": "The net input refers to the total input received by a recurrent unit in a neural network, which is a combination of external inputs and feedback from other units.|Here is another description: The net input refers to the total input received by a neuron or processing unit in a neural network, which is a crucial factor in determining the output of that unit.|Here is another description: The net input refers to the total input received by a memory cell in a neural network, which is crucial for determining the cell's activation and subsequent processing.|Here is another description: The net input, denoted as net input, is a key parameter in the functioning of the memory cell. It is the value that, when equated to netcj[v][t], helps in determining the internal state and output activation of the memory cell at a given time t.|Here is another description: The net input refers to the total input received by a neuron or processing unit in a neural network, which is crucial for determining the activation level of that unit."},
{"net_input__tends_to__perturb_the_stored_information": "The phrase \"tends to\" indicates a general tendency or propensity of the net input to have a certain effect on the system, in this case, affecting the stored information within the recurrent unit."},
{"perturb_the_stored_information": "The stored information refers to the data or patterns that a recurrent unit in a neural network is designed to retain over time. When the net input perturbs this information, it means that the incoming signals disrupt or alter the existing data, making it difficult for the unit to maintain long-term storage of information."},
