{"fully_connected": "The object 'fully connected' describes the type of neural network where each unit is connected to every other unit. This means there are no constraints on the connections between the units within the network.|Here is another description: \"Fully connected\" describes a configuration where every neuron in the hidden layer is connected to every neuron in the preceding and succeeding layers. This means there are no restrictions on the connections, allowing for a dense network of interactions between layers.|Here is another description: Being \"fully connected\" means that every unit in the hidden layer is connected to every other unit in the network, including input units, memory cells, and gate units. This full connectivity allows for comprehensive information flow and interaction between different parts of the network.|Here is another description: Being fully connected means that every unit in the hidden layer is connected to every other unit within the same layer, allowing for complex interactions and information flow between units.|Here is another description: Being \"fully connected\" means that every neuron in the hidden layer is connected to every neuron in the adjacent layers (input and output layers). This full connectivity allows for complex interactions and transformations of the input data as it passes through the network."},
