{"bptt": "BPTT, or Backpropagation Through Time, is a method used in training recurrent neural networks. It involves applying the backpropagation algorithm to a network that has been unfolded over time, allowing the network to learn from sequences of inputs.|Here is another description: BPTT, or Backpropagation Through Time, is a method used in training recurrent neural networks. It is an extension of the backpropagation algorithm to handle sequences of inputs and outputs.|Here is another description: BPTT, or Backpropagation Through Time, is a training algorithm for recurrent neural networks that calculates gradients by unrolling the network through time. It is used to update the weights of the network based on the error at the end of a sequence, allowing the network to learn from temporal dependencies in the data.|Here is another description: BPTT refers to Backpropagation Through Time, a method used in training recurrent neural networks. It is specifically designed to handle the temporal dependencies in sequence prediction problems.|Here is another description: BPTT, or Backpropagation Through Time, is a method used in training recurrent neural networks. It involves unfolding the network through time and applying backpropagation to compute gradients for weight updates."},
{"bptt__is_too_sensitive_to__recent_distractions": "The phrase \"is too sensitive to\" indicates a relationship where the subject, BPTT, exhibits an exaggerated or disproportionate response to the object, in this case, recent distractions. This suggests that BPTT may be adversely affected by minor or temporary changes or inputs."},
