{"cec": "CEC, or Constant Error Carousel, is a key component in the architecture of Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks. It is designed to maintain and propagate errors consistently through the network, enhancing the model's ability to learn long-term dependencies.|Here is another description: The constant error carousel (CEC) is a mechanism within the Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) network that ensures the preservation of error gradients over time, crucial for the network's learning process.|Here is another description: The CEC (Central Error Carrier) is a key component in the architecture designed to maintain a constant error flow through special, self-connected units. It is extended from a basic form to include additional features that enhance its functionality.|Here is another description: The CEC (Constant Error Carrousel) is a self-connected, linear unit designed to allow constant error flow through special units, as described in section 3.2 of the context. It forms the core of the memory cell architecture.|Here is another description: CEC, or the memory cell, is a component within the architecture that stores and processes information, with its functionality significantly influenced by the self-recurrent connection.|Here is another description: The CEC, or Central Executive Component, is a fundamental part of the memory cell's architecture, responsible for processing and managing information flow within the system."},
