{"input_and_output_weight_conflicts": "Input and output weight conflicts refer to the challenges that arise when the weights assigned to inputs and outputs in a system are in conflict, leading to potential issues in the system's performance.|Here is another description: Input and output weight conflicts refer to the challenges that arise when there are discrepancies or inconsistencies between the weights assigned to inputs and outputs in a system. These conflicts can lead to perturbations in stored information and affect the performance of the system, particularly in learning scenarios."},
