{"stored_information": "Stored information refers to data or knowledge that has been saved and retained within a system or memory. In the context of learning and neural networks, this could mean the patterns, weights, or configurations that have been established and need to be maintained over time."},
{"stored_information__must_be_protected_against__perturbation_for_longer_and_longer_periods": "The phrase \"must be protected against\" indicates a necessity for safeguarding or defending stored information from potential disruptions or interferences. This protection is crucial to ensure the integrity and reliability of the stored data, especially as the time lag between input and output increases."},
{"perturbation_for_longer_and_longer_periods": "Perturbation for longer and longer periods refers to the continuous and extended exposure to disturbances or disruptions that can affect stored information. As time progresses, the duration and intensity of these perturbations may increase, making it more challenging to maintain the stability and accuracy of the stored data."},
