{"cec__embodied_by__self_connected_linear_unit_j": "The predicate \"embodied by\" indicates that the CEC is represented or manifested through the self-connected, linear unit _j_. This unit is central to the CEC's operation and is a fundamental part of its structure."},
{"self_connected_linear_unit_j": "The self-connected, linear unit _j_ is a basic building block in the CEC architecture. It is a linear unit with a fixed self-connection, meaning it has a direct feedback loop to itself, which is crucial for maintaining constant error flow. This unit forms the core around which additional features like input and output gates are built."},
{"cec__extended_by__additional_features": "The phrase \"extended by\" indicates that the CEC has been augmented or enhanced with new components or features to improve its functionality and address certain disadvantages of the naive approach."},
