{"multiplicative_input_gate_unit": "The multiplicative input gate unit is a component introduced in the architecture to enhance the functionality of memory cells. It is designed to work alongside a central linear unit with a fixed self-connection, known as the Constant Error Carousel (CEC)."},
{"multiplicative_input_gate_unit__introduced_to__protect_memory_contents_from_perturbation_by_irrelevant_inputs": "The predicate \"introduced to\" signifies the action of adding the multiplicative input gate unit into the architecture. This addition is aimed at improving the system by addressing specific issues related to memory cell perturbations."},
{"protect_memory_contents_from_perturbation_by_irrelevant_inputs": "The object \"protect memory contents from perturbation by irrelevant inputs\" describes the purpose of the multiplicative input gate unit. It is intended to safeguard the memory contents stored within the memory cells from being disturbed or altered by inputs that are not relevant to the current context or task."},
{"multiplicative_output_gate_unit": "The multiplicative output gate unit is a component introduced in the architecture of memory cells to manage the flow of information. It is designed to work alongside a central linear unit with a fixed self-connection, interacting with both an input gate and an output gate to regulate memory content."},
{"multiplicative_output_gate_unit__introduced_to__protect_other_units_from_perturbation_by_currently_irrelevant_memory_contents": "The predicate \"introduced to\" signifies the addition of the multiplicative output gate unit into the memory cell architecture. This introduction aims to enhance the system's ability to maintain constant error flow while mitigating the adverse effects of irrelevant memory contents."},
{"protect_other_units_from_perturbation_by_currently_irrelevant_memory_contents": "Protecting other units from perturbation by currently irrelevant memory contents is a critical function within the memory cell architecture. This protection ensures that the memory cell can store and retrieve relevant information efficiently without being disrupted by extraneous data."},
{"resulting_unit": "The resulting unit is a more complex structure that is developed by extending the CEC embodied by the self-connected, linear unit _j_. It incorporates additional features such as multiplicative input and output gate units to manage memory contents and protect from perturbations."},
{"resulting_unit__called__memory_cell": "The predicate \"called\" signifies the naming or designation of the resulting unit after the introduction of additional features and gate units. It indicates that the unit has been given a specific term to identify its function and structure within the architecture."},
{"memory_cell": "The object \"memory cell\" refers to the designated name of the resulting unit after the enhancements. A memory cell is a central component in the architecture, built around a linear unit with a fixed self-connection and equipped with input and output gate units to manage memory contents effectively.|Here is another description: The memory cell is a component within a neural network, specifically in architectures like Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks, designed to retain information over extended periods. It plays a crucial role in managing and modulating the flow of information, helping the network to learn and remember over long sequences.|Here is another description: The memory cell is a component in a neural network, specifically within the context of recurrent neural networks like LSTMs, that is designed to retain information over long periods, helping the network to remember past inputs and their effects on the current state."},
{"j_th_memory_cell": "The _j_th memory cell is a specialized unit within an architecture designed to maintain constant error flow through self-connected units. It is an extension of the CEC (Constant Error Carrousel) embodied by the self-connected, linear unit _j_, enhanced with additional features to improve functionality."},
