{"cj": "The notation _cj_ is used to denote the _j_th memory cell in a described architecture, which is a complex unit built around a central linear unit with a fixed self-connection, known as the Constant Error Carrousel (CEC). This notation is crucial for understanding the interactions and functions within the system, as it helps in distinguishing this memory cell from others and allows for constant error flow through special, self-connected units."},
{"each_memory_cell": "Each memory cell is a complex unit designed to store and manage memory contents effectively, incorporating features to protect stored information and regulate its flow."},
