{"cj__gets_input_from__multiplicative_unit_inj_the_input_gate": "The predicate \"gets input from\" indicates that the memory cell _cj_ receives input signals. This input is crucial for the functioning of the memory cell, as it allows the cell to integrate information from various sources, including gate units, to modulate its activity and memory contents."},
{"multiplicative_unit_inj_the_input_gate": "The object, \"multiplicative unit _inj_ (the input gate),\" is a component within the memory cell architecture. This input gate unit is designed to protect the memory contents stored in the memory cell from being perturbed by irrelevant inputs. It does so by modulating the input signals that the memory cell receives, ensuring that only relevant information influences the cell's state."},
