{"successful_run__criterion__maximal_absolute_error_of_all_output_units_is_always_below_0_25_after_training_during_10_000_successive_randomly_chosen_input_sequences": "The criterion represents the specific condition or set of conditions that must be satisfied for a run to be considered successful. In this context, it defines the performance threshold that the training process must meet."},
{"maximal_absolute_error_of_all_output_units_is_always_below_0_25_after_training_during_10_000_successive_randomly_chosen_input_sequences": "The maximal absolute error of all output units being always below 0.25 after training during 10,000 successive, randomly chosen input sequences is the specific performance metric and condition that must be met for a run to be deemed successful. This means that the model's predictions must not deviate by more than 0.25 from the true values across all output units for 10,000 consecutive input sequences."},
