{"h__is__identity_function": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies that _h_ is defined as or operates as an identity function within the LSTM framework."},
{"identity_function": "The identity function, denoted as _h_ in this context, is a mathematical function that returns the same value that is input into it. Specifically, for any input _x_, the function _h(x)_ equals _x_.|Here is another description: The object, the identity function, is a mathematical function that returns the same value that is input into it. In the context of neural networks, using the identity function (denoted as _id_) means that the output of a layer is directly proportional to its input without any transformation, which can be a setting for certain types of layers or gates within the network."},
{"h_x": "The subject, _h(x)_, refers to the identity function used in the context of LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) networks. This function is applied to the input data within the memory cell and input gate mechanisms of the LSTM.|Here is another description: The subject _h(x)_ represents a mathematical function that is being defined or described in the context."},
