{"other_methods": "\"Other methods\" refers to alternative techniques or algorithms used in the context, such as BPTT (Backpropagation Through Time) and RTRL (Real-Time Recurrent Learning), which were less effective in learning the task compared to LSTM."},
{"hierarchical_chunker": "The hierarchical chunker is a type of algorithm or model designed to process and organize data into chunks or segments in a hierarchical manner. It is used to efficiently handle and solve complex tasks by breaking them down into manageable parts."},
{"hierarchical_chunker__can_always_quickly_solve_the_task__schmidhuber_1992c_1993": "The phrase \"can always quickly solve the task\" indicates that the hierarchical chunker is highly effective and reliable in addressing the specific task at hand. It suggests that the chunker not only consistently achieves successful outcomes but does so in a timely and efficient manner."},
{"schmidhuber_1992c_1993": "The object \"(Schmidhuber, 1992c, 1993)\" refers to the works of Schmidhuber published in 1992 and 1993. These publications likely detail the development, methodology, and application of the hierarchical chunker, providing the foundational research and context for its capabilities and effectiveness in solving tasks."},
