{"memory_cells_and_gate_units": "Memory cells and gate units are components within the hidden layer of a neural network architecture. They are designed to store and regulate information flow within the network.|Here is another description: Memory cells and gate units are components within a three-layer neural network architecture, specifically within the hidden layer. They are designed to process and manage inputs to facilitate the network's learning and storage capabilities.|Here is another description: Memory cells and gate units, as objects in this context, are the same entities as the subject. They are part of the hidden layer in the neural network, fully connected to each other, and play a vital role in the network's ability to store and process information.|Here is another description: Memory cells and gate units are components within a neural network architecture, specifically designed to manage and process information flow. They play a crucial role in the network's ability to store and manipulate data over time."},
