{"bias_weights": "Bias weights are additional parameters in neural networks that help adjust the activation function's output, providing more flexibility in fitting the data.|Here is another description: Bias weights are parameters within the LSTM architecture that are added to the weighted sum of inputs to a neuron, helping to shift the activation function and allowing the network to fit the data better by providing an additional degree of freedom.|Here is another description: Bias weights in the context of LSTM architecture are parameters that are added to the input of a gate unit to shift the activation function. They help in fine-tuning the gate's decision-making process by providing an additional degree of flexibility in how inputs are processed.|Here is another description: Bias weights are parameters in a neural network that allow the activation function to shift, enabling the model to fit the data better. They are added to the sum of the inputs of a neuron before applying the activation function.|Here is another description: Bias weights are parameters within a neural network that allow the model to fit the data more accurately by providing an additional degree of freedom for each neuron. In this context, bias weights are included in all noninput units, enhancing their ability to learn and adapt to the input signals they process."},
