{"task_3c": "Task 3c is a specific machine learning task within a series of tasks, characterized by its unique architecture, parameters, and the introduction of Gaussian noise on the targets. It requires the system to learn the conditional expectations of the targets given the inputs to minimize mean squared error.|Here is another description: Task 3c is a specific machine learning task that involves an architecture and parameters similar to Task 3a, but with added complexity due to the introduction of Gaussian noise on the targets.|Here is another description: Task 3c is a specific machine learning task that involves an architecture and parameters similar to task 3a, but with added complexity. It requires the system to learn conditional expectations of targets given inputs, despite the presence of Gaussian noise on the targets.|Here is another description: Task 3c is a specific machine learning task that involves predicting targets with added Gaussian noise. It requires the system to learn the conditional expectations of the targets given the inputs to minimize mean squared error."},
{"task_3c__has_targets__0_2_for_class_1_and_0_8_for_class_2": "The predicate \"has_targets\" indicates that Task 3c is defined by specific target values that the system aims to predict. These targets are crucial for evaluating the performance of the system in terms of classification accuracy and mean absolute difference."},
