{"network_output": "The network output refers to the result produced by the neural network after processing the inputs. In this context, it is evaluated based on its accuracy in approximating the conditional expectations of the targets given the inputs, despite the presence of Gaussian noise."},
{"network_output__is_acceptable_if__mean_absolute_difference_between_noise_free_target_and_output_is_below_0_015": "The predicate \"is_acceptable_if\" indicates a condition that must be met for the network output to be deemed satisfactory. Specifically, it relates to the precision and accuracy of the network's predictions in the presence of noise."},
