{"memory_cell_output__is_fed_back_to__its_own_input": "The phrase \"is fed back to\" describes a process where the output of a system is redirected as input back into the same system, creating a feedback loop. This mechanism allows the system to incorporate its previous outputs into its current processing, which can be crucial for maintaining state or memory over time."},
{"its_own_input": "Its own input refers to the input of the same memory cell that produced the output. In the context of neural networks, this means that the output of the memory cell is used as input for the same cell in subsequent processing steps, enabling the cell to retain and update information over time."},
