{"col_2__represents__training_exemplar_selection": "The term \"represents\" in this context indicates that Col. 2 serves as a descriptor or identifier for the method of training exemplar selection used in the dataset. It conveys that the values in Col. 2 correspond to different strategies for selecting training data."},
{"training_exemplar_selection": "Training exemplar selection refers to the process of choosing specific examples from a dataset to be used in training a machine learning model. In this context, it involves methods like randomly selecting from the training set, choosing from two classes, or generating data online."},
{"t_1__stands_for__randomly_chosen_form_training_set": "The predicate \"stands for\" indicates that _t_ 1 is an abbreviation or shorthand notation representing a specific method or condition within the context of training exemplar selection."},
{"randomly_chosen_form_training_set": "The object \"randomly chosen form training set\" describes the method by which training exemplars are selected for task _t_ 1, where the selection is made randomly from the available training set."},
{"t_2__stands_for__randomly_chosen_from_two_classes": "\"stands for\" is a relational phrase indicating that _t_ 2 is an abbreviation or symbolic representation of a specific process or method. In this context, it clarifies the meaning behind the notation _t_ 2."},
{"randomly_chosen_from_two_classes": "\"randomly chosen from two classes\" describes a method of selecting training exemplars where each exemplar is randomly picked from one of two predefined classes. This approach is used to ensure a balanced and random distribution of training data across the classes."},
{"t_3": "_t_ 3 is a task number in a series of training exemplar selections, specifically denoting a particular method used in the process."},
